<p>If you're running Arhc Linux, it's <em>really</em> easy to set up Home
Assistant. No need to bother with Docker containers, just install
<em>one</em> package and you're all set.</p>
<h2>Install</h2>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code># pacman -S home-assistant
</code></pre></div>

<h2>Enable and start</h2>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code># systemctl enable home-assistant
# systemctl start home-assistant
</code></pre></div>

<h2>Enjoy!</h2>
<p>Give Home Assistant a minute or two and head over to
http://localhost:8123/ and start configuring your smart home.</p>